  "title": "Skin lesion localization",
  "description": "Skin lesion localization is a procedure where your doctor marks or identifies a suspicious skin lesion's exact location to guide surgical removal or biopsy. This is particularly helpful for small or difficult-to-see lesions. Your doctor may use a dye injection, wire placement, or radioactive tracer to mark the lesion. This type of procedure can be performed various ways, including without mammography and with mammography, and the cost may vary depending on the specific approach or service provided.",
